  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "Use-after-free caused by storing a pointer from a transient DXF pair into a TABLEGEOMETRY object, then freeing that pair. In TABLEGEOMETRY decoding (dwg.spec generated code), SUB_FIELD_HANDLE(cell, tablegeometry, ...) assigns cell.tablegeometry from the current Dxf_Pair data. In new_object(), each loop iteration immediately calls dxf_free_pair(pair) and reads the next pair. That leaves cell.tablegeometry dangling. Later, during cleanup, dwg_free_TABLEGEOMETRY_private dereferences/frees this stale handle pointer, triggering heap-use-after-free at dwg.spec:7277 path.",
    "conditions": "Via llvmfuzz, a crafted DXF BLOCKS section containing a TABLEGEOMETRY object with group code 330 (cell.tablegeometry handle) causes new_object() to parse and assign the handle from pair memory. Because pair is freed each iteration (dxf_free_pair at in_dxf.c:11818), TABLEGEOMETRY retains a dangling reference. When LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput calls dwg_free(), object destruction reaches dwg_free_TABLEGEOMETRY_private and reads that freed handle, producing the ASan UAF. Input must reach TABLEGEOMETRY parsing and include relevant cell/handle fields (e.g., 92/93/330)."
  },
